# Cleaning up after testing various API calls

```elixir
Mix.install([
  # {:openai_ex, "~> 0.9.22"},
  {:openai_ex, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")}
])
```

## Setup

Every cell below deletes **all** resources of one type in the project the API key belongs to, not only the ones the user guide created. Run it only against a test project.

```elixir
apikey = System.fetch_env!("LB_OPENAI_API_KEY")
openai = OpenaiEx.new(apikey) |> OpenaiEx.with_receive_timeout(60_000)
```

`sweep` lists a resource type, deletes what it finds, and repeats until the list is empty. A list can still show a deleted item for a few seconds, so a failed delete stops the sweep instead of looping.

```elixir
sweep = fn list, delete ->
  Stream.repeatedly(fn ->
    {:ok, %{"data" => items}} = list.()
    Enum.map(items, &(&1["id"] |> delete.() |> elem(0)))
  end)
  |> Enum.reduce_while(%{ok: 0, error: 0}, fn
    [], acc -> {:halt, acc}
    results, acc ->
      acc = Enum.reduce(results, acc, &Map.update!(&2, &1, fn n -> n + 1 end))
      if Enum.any?(results, &(&1 == :ok)), do: {:cont, acc}, else: {:halt, acc}
  end)
end
```

## Agents cleanup

```elixir
alias OpenaiEx.Beta.Agents

%{
  sessions: sweep.(fn -> Agents.Sessions.list(openai, %{limit: 100}) end, &Agents.Sessions.delete(openai, &1)),
  agents: sweep.(fn -> Agents.list(openai, %{limit: 100}) end, &Agents.delete(openai, &1)),
  vaults: sweep.(fn -> Agents.Vaults.list(openai, %{limit: 100}) end, &Agents.Vaults.delete(openai, &1)),
  templates:
    sweep.(
      fn -> Agents.Environments.Templates.list(openai, %{limit: 100}) end,
      &Agents.Environments.Templates.delete(openai, &1)
    )
}
```

## Evals cleanup

```elixir
sweep.(fn -> OpenaiEx.Evals.list(openai, %{limit: 100}) end, &OpenaiEx.Evals.delete(openai, &1))
```

## Containers cleanup

Containers created by the Responses code interpreter tool stay listed as `expired` until they are deleted.

```elixir
sweep.(fn -> OpenaiEx.Containers.list(openai, %{limit: 100}) end, &OpenaiEx.Containers.delete(openai, &1))
```

## Vector Stores cleanup

```elixir
sweep.(fn -> OpenaiEx.VectorStores.list(openai) end, &OpenaiEx.VectorStores.delete(openai, &1))
```

## Files cleanup

```elixir
sweep.(fn -> OpenaiEx.Files.list(openai) end, &OpenaiEx.Files.delete(openai, &1))
```

## Stored Chat Completions cleanup

```elixir
sweep.(
  fn -> OpenaiEx.Chat.Completions.list(openai, limit: 100) end,
  &OpenaiEx.Chat.Completions.delete(openai, completion_id: &1)
)
```

## Check

Each list should now be empty. A deleted item can linger in a list for a few seconds, so re-run this cell if one is not.

```elixir
for {name, list} <- [
      agent_sessions: fn -> Agents.Sessions.list(openai) end,
      agents: fn -> Agents.list(openai) end,
      vaults: fn -> Agents.Vaults.list(openai) end,
      evals: fn -> OpenaiEx.Evals.list(openai) end,
      containers: fn -> OpenaiEx.Containers.list(openai) end,
      vector_stores: fn -> OpenaiEx.VectorStores.list(openai) end,
      files: fn -> OpenaiEx.Files.list(openai) end,
      chat_completions: fn -> OpenaiEx.Chat.Completions.list(openai) end
    ],
    into: %{} do
  {:ok, %{"data" => items}} = list.()
  {name, length(items)}
end
```
